y a:","value":"Long narrative poem","group":"Language & Literature","major":"Language & Literature","era":"Other","relation":"term function","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epic_poetry","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Epic poetry narrates major deeds and adventures, often involving foundational heroes.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04395","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4396","nodeId":"REVISION85-4396","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Cuneiform writing first developed in:","value":"Mesopotamia","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuneiform","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Cuneiform originated in southern Mesopotamia, initially in the Sumerian cultural sphere.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04396","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4397","nodeId":"REVISION85-4397","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Phoenicians are especially associated with the spread of:","value":"An alphabet","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phoenician_alphabet","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Their consonantal alphabet influenced later Mediterranean writing systems, including Greek.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04397","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4398","nodeId":"REVISION85-4398","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Persian Wars were fought between the Persian Empire and:","value":"Greek city-states","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greco-Persian_Wars","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Greek coalitions resisted Achaemenid Persian invasions.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04398","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4399","nodeId":"REVISION85-4399","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Pericles is most closely associated with the political life of:","value":"Athens","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pericles","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Pericles led Athens during much of its fifth-century BCE cultural and political high point.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04399","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4400","nodeId":"REVISION85-4400","anchor":"ENT:ALEXANDER-THE-GREAT","subject":"Alexander the Great was king of:","value":"Macedon","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_the_Great","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Alexander inherited the Macedonian kingdom before conquering the Persian Empire.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04400","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4401","nodeId":"REVISION85-4401","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Punic Wars were fought between Rome and:","value":"Carthage","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punic_Wars","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"The three wars established Roman dominance over Carthage and the western Mediterranean.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04401","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4402","nodeId":"REVISION85-4402","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Gracchi are especially associated with proposals for:","value":"Land reform","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gracchi","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Tiberius and Gaius Gracchus sought reforms including changes to the distribution of public land.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04402","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4403","nodeId":"REVISION85-4403","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"Julius Caesar's crossing of the Rubicon initiated a:","value":"Civil war","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crossing_the_Rubicon","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Crossing into Italy with his army challenged senatorial authority and began civil war.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04403","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4404","nodeId":"REVISION85-4404","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The battle of Actium was a:","value":"Naval battle","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Actium","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Octavian's forces defeated those of Antony and Cleopatra at sea.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04404","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4405","nodeId"