 Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austro-Prussian_War","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Prussia's victory excluded Austria from the subsequent German unification process.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04421","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4422","nodeId":"REVISION85-4422","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The assassination that triggered the July Crisis of 1914 took place in:","value":"Sarajevo","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assassination_of_Archduke_Franz_Ferdinand","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Archduke Franz Ferdinand was assassinated in Sarajevo.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04422","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4423","nodeId":"REVISION85-4423","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Western Front in the First World War is especially associated with:","value":"Trench warfare","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references":[{"file":"Original general-knowledge question: topic reference","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Front_(World_War_I)","checkedOnline85":false}],"explanation74":"Long systems of trenches characterised much of the fighting on the Western Front.","questionId85":"GEN43-Q04423","reviewStatus85":"ready"},{"id":"REVISION85-4424","nodeId":"REVISION85-4424","anchor":"MAJOR:HISTORY-AND-POLITICS","subject":"The Bolsheviks came to power in Russia under the leadership of:","value":"Lenin","group":"History & Politics","major":"History & Politics","era":"Other","relation":"context relation","references"